}

body:json {
  {
    "text": "Is my son on track for his reading goal this year?",
    "about": "goal:340"
  }
}

docs {
  # POST /api/advocate/threads/{id}/messages

  Sends a parent message and streams the advocate's answer back as **server-sent events**
  (`Content-Type: text/event-stream; charset=utf-8`). Rate limited by the `advocate-message`
  policy (30 requests / 15 minutes per user).

  Bruno does not render SSE incrementally: the response pane fills in once the stream closes, and
  a long answer can take tens of seconds. The raw body shows the frames below.

  ## Body (`SendAdvocateMessageRequest`)

  - `text` (required) — 1–2000 characters.
  - `about` (optional, max 40) — launcher context in the form `<kind>:<id>` where kind is
    `iep | etr | goal | analysis | progress_report | journal` (e.g. `iep:12`, `goal:340`).
    Unrecognised values are ignored.

  ## Before the stream starts (plain JSON `ApiResponse`)

  Failures that can be decided before the model is called come back as ordinary status codes:

  - `400` — validation (empty / over-limit text)
  - `401` — missing/invalid bearer token
  - `403` — forbidden
  - `404` — thread not found or not owned by the caller
  - `429` — usage cap reached (`message` explains the cap), or the `advocate-message` rate limit
  - `500` — the advocate is unavailable before any frame could be produced

  ## Stream (`200`, `text/event-stream`)

  Each frame is `event: <name>\ndata: <json>\n\n`. JSON is camelCase with nulls omitted. Comment
  lines `: ping` are written every 15 seconds while the model is busy and should be ignored.

  ```
  event: tool
  data: {"name":"get_goal_progress","label":"Reading goal progress","status":"started"}

  event: tool
  data: {"name":"get_goal_progress","label":"Reading goal progress","status":"finished"}

  event: delta
  data: {"text":"Based on the latest progress report, "}

  event: delta
  data: {"text":"your son has moved from 45 to 68 words per minute ..."}

  event: done
  data: {"messageId":41,"contentMarkdown":"Based on the latest progress report, your son has ...","citations":[{"kind":"goal","id":340,"label":"Reading fluency","parent":{"kind":"iep","id":12}}],"suggestions":[{"kind":"prep_question","text":"How is fluency being measured each week?"}],"truncated":false,"disclaimer":"The Virtual Advocate gives general information ... It is not legal advice. ..."}
  ```

  Frames:

  - `delta` — `{ text }`: the next chunk of the answer; concatenate deltas in order.
  - `tool` — `{ name, label, status }`: a record lookup the advocate is running; `status` is `started | finished | failed`.
  - `done` — `{ messageId, contentMarkdown, citations[], suggestions[], truncated, disclaimer }`: the persisted assistant message. `contentMarkdown` is the authoritative full text (use it instead of the concatenated deltas). `citations` / `suggestions` have the same shape as in *Get advocate thread with messages*. `truncated` is true when the answer hit its length budget. Terminal frame.
  - `error` — `{ code, message }`: a failure after the stream started; `code` is `unavailable` and `message` is safe to show. Terminal frame. (`validation | not_found | forbidden | usage_cap` are never streamed — they are returned as the status codes above before the stream begins.)
}
